Release the queued argument reference before replacing a destroyed proxy with
null. destroy_queued_closure cannot release it after the pointer has been cleared.
Local fix against the MIT-licensed Wayland 1.26.0 release; not an upstream claim.
See docs/verification/R062b-wayland-proxy.md for the independent reproducer.

--- a/src/wayland-client.c
+++ b/src/wayland-client.c
@@ -265,8 +265,10 @@ validate_closure_objects(struct wl_closure *closure)
 		case WL_ARG_NEW_ID:
 		case WL_ARG_OBJECT:
 			proxy = (struct wl_proxy *) closure->args[i].o;
-			if (proxy && proxy->flags & WL_PROXY_FLAG_DESTROYED)
+			if (proxy && proxy->flags & WL_PROXY_FLAG_DESTROYED) {
 				closure->args[i].o = NULL;
+				wl_proxy_unref(proxy);
+			}
 			break;
 		default:
 			break;
